0 Ackermann Car
0 Name: ackermann-car.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // A wide car with Ackermann steering. Each front wheel turns on its own kingpin, steered by an
0 // arm that points back and in, at the middle of the rear axle; links on ball joints join the
0 // arms to a rack, moved by a pinion on the steering column. On a turn the inner wheel turns
0 // further than the outer one, so all four wheels roll round the same centre. The rear wheels
0 // are on a differential. Front is +x. Wheelbase 400 LDU, track 487 LDU, hubs at y = -38.

0 // Step 1: the chassis, a 6x24 plate
1 72 180 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3026.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: the rear differential, its output axles and bevel gears (as in differential.ldr),
0 // on a 1x6 brick with a Technic 1x6 brick on top each side
1 14 20 -24 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 20 -24 -50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 20 -48 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
1 14 20 -48 -50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
